      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. but looking at the actual facts of the timeline, some people argue that the zionist movement was essentially a colonial project because it was backed by the british empire, whereas the palestinian side was just trying to defend their existing home. from a historical perspective, would you say there's a way to look at the conflict where one side's claims are seen as more legitimate or fundamentally grounded in international law than the other?",
